From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon W. Jackson <simonwjackson@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 May 2026 22:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Input: edt-ft5x06 - honour DT 'input-name' property

When two ft5x06 controllers share an SoC (e.g. AYN Thor's
dual-touchscreen design with one ft5426 on i2c4 driving the top panel
and one ft5452 on i2c-hub-3 driving the bottom panel), both expose
vendor=0 product=0 to libinput and the driver names both input devices
"generic ft5x06 (8d)" because the chip-id-based model detection falls
through to the same generic branch.

Wayland compositors that build input identifiers as
vendor:product:name (sway / wlroots, in particular) cannot tell the
two controllers apart and have no escape syntax for path-based
identifiers, so per-device 'map_to_output' rules become impossible
and one panel's touch events can end up routed to the wrong surface.

Allow the devicetree to override input->name via a new optional
'input-name' property. When present, it wins over the chip-detected
model name. Existing devicetree blobs that don't set the property
keep their current behaviour.

Signed-off-by: Simon W. Jackson <simonwjackson@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c
@@ -1348,7 +1348,14 @@
 		"Model \"%s\", Rev. \"%s\", %dx%d sensors\n",
 		tsdata->name, tsdata->fw_version, tsdata->num_x, tsdata->num_y);
 
-	input->name = tsdata->name;
+	/*
+	 * Allow devicetree to override the input device name. Lets boards
+	 * with multiple ft5x06 controllers (which all otherwise report the
+	 * same chip-detected model name) hand Wayland compositors distinct
+	 * vendor:product:name identifiers for per-device routing.
+	 */
+	if (device_property_read_string(&client->dev, "input-name", &input->name))
+		input->name = tsdata->name;
 	input->id.bustype = BUS_I2C;
 	input->dev.parent = &client->dev;
 
-- 
